page('01 / Research question and competing explanations',[
P('The course brief asks whether measured economic narratives help explain the difference between US sentiment and economic conditions [1]. We test that question without assuming irrational consumers or biased negative reporting.'),
T([['Required question','Answer supported by this design'],['1. How can bias be measured?','Compare tone, wording, selection, and numerical claims with a defined event or factual benchmark. Negative tone alone is insufficient.'],['2. Impact on Michigan sentiment?','Controlled regressions estimate associations. Exposure data are absent, so a national causal impact is unidentified.'],['3. What do U3, PCE, and GDP explain?','The long-sample model has adjusted R-squared 0.477. Its average gap since 2022 is -14.85 points. Neither number is a causal explained share.'],['4. Which perceptual mechanisms are measurable?','We measure supplied language and topic emphasis. Reader anchoring, selective exposure, recall, and confirmation bias remain unmeasured.'],['5. Does media improve prediction?','A small-sample M1 improvement disappears in controlled comparisons. A dictionary sensitivity supplies conflicting exploratory evidence.'],['6. What contradicts a media-bias explanation?','Accurate favorable news, attenuation with controls, weak changes, and poor incremental forecasts challenge a simple explanation.']],[150,345]),
P('Theory and falsification','Sub'),P('Household experience predicts that cumulative costs and purchasing power add information beyond annual inflation and GDP. A distinct media signal predicts a contribution after these controls. Model or survey differences predict sensitivity to dynamics, timing, and survey eras.'),
P('These explanations overlap. News can transmit genuine household pressures. Controlling for those pressures can absorb part of that channel. Attenuation therefore limits a simple media claim but does not identify the causal alternative.'),
P('Earlier versions inspected the evaluation years. The written audit design freezes this correction, but it is not a preregistration or an untouched confirmation. We retain unfavorable results and do not select a method to obtain significance.')])
